From 67c821eb13a795b5bc063b34ddaf2fe3c8522a48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rfishback <rfishback@anduril.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 12:59:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] overlay: imx708: add binned and binned-cropped mode entries
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extend the IMX708 overlays to advertise three modes per camera:

- mode0: 4608x2592 @ 14 fps  (line_length 4808, pix_clk 297.6 MHz)
- mode1: 2304x1296 @ 56 fps  (line_length 7824, pix_clk 585.6 MHz)
- mode2: 1536x864  @ 90 fps  (line_length 5216, pix_clk 566.4 MHz)

mode0 timing matches RidgeRun's working JP6.0 values unchanged.
mode1 and mode2 use RPi imx708's native pixel_rate and line_length_pix
constants directly — same convention as IMX219 in jetpack-nixos
(IMX219_PIXEL_RATE = 182400000 mirrored verbatim into pix_clk_hz).
Keeping pclk_dt / ll_dt aligned with the sensor's actual lines/sec
gives the VI/CSI capture path the timing model the sensor really runs.

mode2 is capped at 90 fps for CSI/VI margin: the sensor can hit ~120 fps
(vblank_min=40 in RPi imx708.c), but Tegracam writes FRM_LENGTH from DT,
so the advertised max is the rate the sensor actually sees.

Updated files:
- tegra234-camera-rbpcv3-imx708.dtsi (shared, both cam0 and cam1)
- tegra234-p3767-camera-p3768-imx708-A.dts (CAM0 single-camera)
- tegra234-p3767-camera-p3768-imx708-C.dts (CAM1 single-camera)
---
